Each panel shows one covariate. The blue points are scaled Schoenfeld residuals at each event time,
the red curve is a loess smooth, and the dashed grey line marks the overall coefficient estimate.
The p-value in each panel title is from the `cox_zph()` test. A flat smooth close to the reference
line confirms proportional hazards; a curve that departs from it reveals where and how the effect
changes.

The time axis can be transformed to spread out events more evenly, which sometimes makes trends
easier to see. Pass `transform="log"` for log time, `transform="km"` for the Kaplan-Meier failure
probability, or `transform="rank"` for time ranks:

