The `df` parameter controls the flexibility of the spline. Higher values allow more wiggly curves.
The default (`df=4`) is a good starting point. The `reference` parameter sets the covariate value
where the log-HR is zero; it defaults to the weighted mean.

::: {#df102c34 .cell execution_count=14}
``` {.python .cell-code}
# A more flexible curve (df=6) with age 50 as the reference
shr6 = cox.smooth_hr("age", df=6, reference=50)
gw.plot_smooth_hr(shr6)
```

